>  <GRAPH_SOURCE>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review

>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1107/S160053680701269X","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/2213019.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Build the graph for the C₂₃H₁₅ input. An additional transannular C–C contact joins two hydrogen-free ring carbons without phenyl substituents, Both Wiberg and Mayer bond orders support retaining the weak bond. The ring system has formal charge −1, Three Cl⁻ balance Ti(IV) together with the ring ligand. The difference between these coordinates and the triphenylcyclopentadienyl species in the original paper is recorded separately. Localized 23 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Missing label

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Not independently verified

