>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Ru–N–O 176.76°, N–O 1.17145 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.7684. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +2 and total charge -1. The authors characterized, IR/NMR, diamagnetism and negative-ion mass spectra in assigning the [MCl₄(NO)(Hazole)]⁻ species to {MNO}⁶. A neutral azole and four Cl⁻ are compatible with M(II)/NO⁺; Adopted as a limiting structure. The CIF designation M(III) is recorded separately. Localized 10 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 22 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 17 nonmetal covalent bonds: 16 within range, 0 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

