>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1039/C5RA03848K","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/7220130.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Each of the two equivalent ligands has a single hydrogen-free carbon between a tetrazole N and the carboxyl group. N–C has partial multiple-bond character, Use the charge-separated N⁺=C⁻ form, Each carboxylate carries −1. Each of four waters has two H atoms, These ligands coordinate Zn(II). Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

